      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-13T02:59:09Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(post): the PathPilot G76 reads the finishing step #417 states\n\nMerging main brought #612's Tormach lathe post, which refused any\nnon-zero FinishAllowance. Under #417 the field is the finishing pass's\nown step (never 0 on a laid ladder), so every LinuxCNC G76 was refused.\nThe post now accepts the step R1's equal ladder takes itself\n(K - (ceil(K/J) - 1)*J) and refuses any other, and an alternating\nrecord, by name.\n\nAlso: ThreadCycle.alternating in the recorded_streams fixture, and the\ninfeed pin asserts rest::prior_digest is equal before the save and\nafter the load (the Stale-after-load seen on another platform is a\nmain defect: the save snaps moves to the 1 um lattice while the path\nsignature hashes the unsnapped ones - reported separately).\n\nRefs #417\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
